WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.890
Landing on Mars takes about seven minutes, and nobody on Earth can help.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:14.650
Radio needs several minutes to cross the gap. By the time the first signal arrives, it's already over.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:24.140
In 1997, Mars Pathfinder bounced to a stop inside giant airbags.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:31.880
In 2012, Curiosity was lowered on cables by a hovering rocket stage: the sky crane.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:38.470
In 2021, Perseverance did it again, and photographed itself on the way down.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:45.980
Heat shield, parachute, rockets: each step slows it down, all on its own.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:53.930
Afterwards, most data from the surface reaches Earth through orbiters passing overhead, acting as relays.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:03.370
Perseverance hit the air at about 20,000 kilometres per hour, and touched down slower than a walk.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:09.260
Now compare your design. In the game, your orbiter carries the call for help.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:14.570
<v Chicho>Nobody gets left behind. Not on Mars, not anywhere.

